Sparky Stereo OS: the 3D view is drawn as a stereo pair, two parallel cameras meeting at the camera's focal distance (Coin's off-axis stereo camera in perspective, a shear about the focal plane in orthographic), into the two buffers of the view's own OpenGL viewport, which the edition's Qt shows as a stereo window of its own and Mesa hands to Stereo KWin as declared full side by side; the rest of the window stays one picture (row 50 step 5).
The separation is the person's depth limits, read from the desktop through libstereo-declare: before the left eye the scene and its annotations are drawn once from the camera between the eyes and their depth read, and the separation is the largest under which every pixel stays inside the limits; a live change of the limits redraws the view; no separation setting (FreeCAD's eye distance is not offered). Without limits both eyes are the same picture and the report view says why, once.
View, Stereo holds Enable 3D (on by default, the person's choice for every 3D view, applied to the open ones) and 3D Display Settings; the red/cyan and interleaved views are not offered (the desktop's display settings make every output), and the Python API's setStereoType keeps Mono and QuadBuffer. Picking, preselection and navigation use the camera between the eyes; the navigation cube, the corner coordinate system, the background and the rubber band are drawn in both eyes at the screen's depth.
The new sentences in the ten languages (translations/freecad-3d-view-stereo.ts.patch). Build-Depends: libstereo-declare-dev (>= 1.12.2), pkgconf, qt6-base-private-dev; libfreecad-python3 depends on qt6-base-private-abi (= the Qt it was built with).
